fix(client): repair workspace archive flow and restore workspace delete (#235)

dsh-tauri-session:
- workspace-patch: resolve the archive target from the clicked project row
  against the runtime snapshot instead of the DOM group heuristic. The
  official browser renders no session rows for collapsed groups, so the old
  ancestor scan either found nothing (all collapsed: archive did nothing)
  or landed on the outer container (mixed: archived the nearest expanded
  workspace instead). Session ids now come from workspace.sessionIds.
- workspace-patch: keep the official "delete workspace" item intact and
  append a separate "archive workspace" item next to it, restoring the
  delete capability that the previous rewrite removed.
- store: clear suppressedSessionIds after a successful archive refresh.
  The suppression is only meant to hide ghost rows during the mutation ->
  refresh window; keeping it forever made a session unarchived and then
  re-archived disappear from both the sidebar and the archive page.

dsh-tauri-rightclick:
- replace native window.confirm with a client-styled primitives Modal for
  workspace/ungrouped archive and the new workspace delete confirmation
  (native confirm renders as the WebView2 "embedded page" banner).
- add a danger "delete workspace" entry to the workspace context menu
  (official non-destructive delete keeps folder and sessions).
